          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 0 ^ { 1 6 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " seconds ≈ 31.7 crore years "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 0 ^ { 1 7 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " seconds "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\approx 3 . 1 7"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " billion years"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.365,
            0.096,
            0.865,
            0.136
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Plants on land started 47 crore/470 million years ago ( ≈ seconds)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.386,
            0.141,
            0.857,
            0.181
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The oldest fossil evidence suggests that bacteria first appeared about 3.7 billion years ago."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.364,
            0.186,
            0.713,
            0.206
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The Earth is 4.5 billion years old."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.364,
            0.213,
            0.843,
            0.271
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The Milky Way galaxy was formed 13.6 billion years ago, and the Universe was formed 13.8 billion years ago."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.289,
            0.849,
            0.365
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Notice that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 0 ^ { 9 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " seconds is of the order of the lifespan of a human, whereas "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 0 ^ { 1 8 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " seconds ago the universe did not exist according to modern physics!! The exponential notation can capture very large quantities in a concise manner."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.375,
            0.701,
            0.397
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Calculate and write the answer using scientific notation:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.189,
            0.399,
            0.847,
            0.455
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) If one star is counted every second, how long would it take to count all the stars in the universe? Answer in terms of the number of seconds using scientific notation."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.185,
            0.455,
            0.819,
            0.511
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) If one could drink a glass of water (200 ml) every 10 seconds, how long would it take to finish the entire volume of water on Earth?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.828,
            0.448,
            0.928,
            0.501
          ],
          "content": [
