            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.194,
            0.533,
            0.822,
            0.61
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Very large quantities are often beyond our experience and comprehension. To put them into perspective, we can relate and compare them with quantities we are familiar with. This can give an essence of how large a number or a measure is!"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.652,
            0.452,
            0.676
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2.5 A Pinch of History"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.685,
            0.848,
            0.759
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In the Lalitavistara, a Buddhist treatise from the first century BCE, we see number -names for odd powers of ten up to "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 0 ^ { 5 3 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . The following occurs as part of the dialogue between the mathematician Arjuna and Prince Gautama, the Bodhisattva."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.759,
            0.847,
            0.834
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "“Hundred kotis are called an ayuta "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "( 1 0 ^ { 9 } )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , hundred ayutas a niyuta "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "( 1 0 ^ { 1 1 } )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " hundred niyutas a kankara "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "( 1 0 ^ { \\bar { 1 } 3 } )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , …, hundred sarva-balas a visamjnagati "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "( 1 0 ^ { 4 7 } )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , hundred visamjna-gatis a sarvajna "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "( 1 0 ^ { 4 9 } )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , hundred sarvajnas a vibhutangama "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "( 1 0 ^ { 5 1 } )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , a hundred vibhutangamas is a tallakshana "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "( 1 0 ^ { 5 3 } )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " ”"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.833,
            0.848,
            0.926
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Mahaviracharya gives a list of 24 terms (i.e., up to "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 0 ^ { 2 3 } )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " in his treatise Ganita-sara-sangraha. An anonymous Jaina treatise Amalasiddhi gives a list with a name for each power of ten up to "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 0 ^ { 9 6 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (dasha-ananta). A Pali grammar treatise of Kāccāyana lists number-names up to "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 0 ^ { 1 4 0 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , named asaṅkhyeya."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.092,
            0.923,
            0.127,
            0.944
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "42"
            }
          ]
        },
